soma verify app.cell → ✓ before Ordo.delivered … via Ordo.consult_of ; soma test app.cell → o1 delivered while its link names c2, never done. `on relink(id, c) { let r = "{consult_of.set(id, c)}" … }` rewrites the link from inside a string's `{…}`: link_written_once (product.rs:1135-1148) walks statements and expressions of the AST, not the segments of an interpolated string (desugar::segment_exprs), so relink is not counted as a writer.
